  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Development of a Concentrated Solar Power Plant</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The project concerns the development of a Concentrated Solar Power Plant in the Hermel-Kaa region (Northern Lebanon). The power sector in Lebanon is known for chronic inefficiencies and shortages in supply reaching up to nine hours per day in some regions, and even more during the peak summer months. With the massive influx of 1.5 million Syrian refugees that require an additional power demand of almost 480 MW, the power shortage gap is further increasing, leaving the country with a higher energy deficit than in 2012.</narrative>
  </description>
